  [codex stderr] +- sampled `__book.json` contains `11` sections with:
  [codex stderr] +  - `approval_status = pending`
  [codex stderr] +  - `verification_status = agent_validated`
  [codex stderr] +- repo search found no script that applies `__approval-decisions.json` back into the book and exports a publish-ready PDF
  [codex stderr] +
  [codex stderr] +Why this matters:
  [codex stderr] +
  [codex stderr] +- Operators can finish the visible review queue and still remain blocked from publish-ready export.
  [codex stderr] +- The repo currently proves generation and review bundle creation, but not the state transition from reviewed content to publish-ready output.
  [codex stderr] +- Section 3 cannot be certified until this path exists and is exercised.
  [codex stderr] +
  [codex stderr] +Required fix direction:
  [codex stderr] +
  [codex stderr] +- Align review queue semantics with export gate semantics, or add an explicit, tested state promotion path for agent-validated sections that still preserves fail-closed behavior.
  [codex stderr] +- Add a deterministic decision-application and publish-ready export command path.
  [codex stderr] +
  [codex stderr] +### SEV-2: PDF heading normalization regression leaks internal section keys
  [codex stderr] +
  [codex stderr] +Status: Open
